      "filename": "Gopuram monumental ornate tower at the entrance of Sri Mariamman Temple with sculptures of Hindu deities Chinatown Singapore.jpg",
      "title": "File:Gopuram monumental ornate tower at the entrance of Sri Mariamman Temple with sculptures of Hindu deities Chinatown Singapore.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Gopuram_monumental_ornate_tower_at_the_entrance_of_Sri_Mariamman_Temple_with_sculptures_of_Hindu_deities_Chinatown_Singapore.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gopuram_monumental_ornate_tower_at_the_entrance_of_Sri_Mariamman_Temple_with_sculptures_of_Hindu_deities_Chinatown_Singapore.jpg",
      "width": 3584,
      "height": 4779,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Basile Morin",
      "description": "Gopuram, monumental ornate entrance tower, at Sri Mariamman Temple, 19th-century Hindu temple, 244 South Bridge Road, Chinatown, Singapore. Built in the South Indian Dravidian style, this gopuram rises above the main entrance along South Bridge Road. It is richly embellished with six tiers of sculptures of Hindu deities, other figures and ornamental decorations. The tower tapers up towards to a moulded ornamental ridge. Flanking the gopuram are a sculpture of Murugan on the right and Krishna on the left (as one enters). The sculptures are all of plaster, which allows for fine detailing. They are painted in a variety of bright colours, which adds to the visual quality of this gopuram.",
      "dateCreated": "2018-06-05 11:44:32",
      "sourceType": "poi",
      "sourceArticleId": "chinatown-singapore-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "w21z",
      "mediumPath": "_m/w/2/1/z/chinatown-singapore-wp/gopuram-monumental-ornate-towe-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/w/2/1/z/chinatown-singapore-wp/gopuram-monumental-ornate-towe-small.webp"
